q4os-welcome (4.4.0-a5) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Automatic login outside Trinity asks for the password through polkit
    (pkexec) instead of tdesudo, so the Qt5 frontend needs no Trinity program
    for it. Trinity keeps tdesudo.
  * q4os-welcome5 depends on pkexec | policykit-1 for that.
  * The menu entry names of both frontends are translated in ten languages
    (Name[xx] lines from the q4os-shortcuts catalog of q4os-i18n).

 -- Q4OS Team <devteam@q4os.org>  Mon, 05 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0200

q4os-welcome (4.4.0-a4) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Documents online, Patreon and Donate check for a web browser first: on a
    system without one the page opened in Kate as HTML source; a short note
    now says to install a browser.
  * Qt5: at a fractional scale factor (Plasma X11 at 125%) the main panel's
    border is drawn by a style sheet, as a QFrame Box loses its top line there.

