 -- Q4OS Team <devteam@q4os.org>  Fri, 25 Sep 2026 21:00:00 +0200

q4os-welcome (4.4.0-a1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * One source for three packages, as q4os-sw-profiler, q4os-cpuq and q4os-updater are
    built: q4os-welcome (the Trinity frontend), q4os-welcome5 (the Plasma frontend, now
    plain Qt5 - no KF5, no q4os-api library - built here instead of from the separate
    generated tree, which is retired) and q4os-welcome-common (icon, header images,
    translations). Everything the buttons do lives in shared/, compiled into both
    frontends, and so does the wording set from code, so the two can no longer drift.
  * Ship the welcome-screen gettext catalog here instead of q4os-i18n, completed in
    18 languages (cs de es es_AR fr he hu id it ja nl pl pt pt_BR ru tr uk zh_CN); the
    .mo files stay in /usr/share/locale and reach TDE's /opt/trinity/share/locale as
    symlinks, so the Trinity frontend is translated as well.
  * Launch the Desktop Profiler through q4os-sw-profiler-common's desktop-profiler
    launcher, which runs the frontend of the running session. No dependency on it: the
    frontend is a hard dependency of the edition's q4os-desktop-* metapackage.
  * q4os-welcome no longer depends on q4os-api (it no longer links its library).
  * Install Applications runs the Software Centre through q4os-swcentre-common's
    session-aware launcher (software-centre) instead of swcentre.exu directly, so a
    Plasma session gets the Qt5 Software Centre (q4os-swcentre5).
  * Qt5 frontend: the designer connections inherited from the KF5 forms are
    removed from form1-3.ui - the classes connect their buttons explicitly, so
    every handler ran TWICE (two Software Centres from one "Install
    Applications" click, found by the a86 session QA).

 -- Q4OS Team <devteam@q4os.org>  Fri, 25 Sep 2026 10:23:22 +0200

q4os-welcome (4.3.3-a1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Suppress the default dh_auto_configure, it breaks the rpi12 build
  * Stop blocking the buttons during NVIDIA/VirtualBox setup
  * Add q4os-api-dev to Build-Depends: q4os-api no longer ships its own
    headers (moved to q4os-api-dev exclusively); no source changes needed
    here, this package still links q4os-api's .so at build time as before.

